Module code with labels after the SUBs of an $INCLUDE file uses a TYPE and DIM SHARED variables the file declares before its first SUB. QB64 rejects labels between SUB/FUNCTIONs; QBasic treats them as module-level code. The compiler moves that code in front of the first SUB inside the included file, after those declarations (it used to land before the $INCLUDE line, ahead of them). Expected output written by hand from QBasic semantics.
